{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <climits>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007;\nvector<int> a(1111111);\nvector<long long> x(30);\nlong long now = 6;\n\nint cal(long long n) {\n    if (n < 0) n = -n;\n    if (n <= now) return a[n];\n    \n    int l = 0;\n    long long last = 0, t = n;\n    while (t > 0) {\n        l++;\n        last = t % 10;\n        t /= 10;\n    }\n    \n    if (last <= 5) {\n        if (n >= x[l] * last || last == 1) {\n            return cal(n - x[l] * last) + last * l;\n        } else {\n            int r1 = cal(x[l] * last - n) + last * l;\n            int r2 = cal(n - x[l] * (last - 1)) + (last - 1) * l;\n            return min(r1, r2);\n        }\n    } else if (last > 6) {\n        return cal(x[l + 1] - n) + l + 1;\n    } else {\n        int r1, r2;\n        if (n > x[l] * last) {\n            r1 = cal(n - x[l] * last) + last * l;\n        } else {\n            r1 = cal(x[l] * last - n) + last * l;\n        }\n        r2 = cal(n - x[l] * (last - 1)) + (last - 1) * l;\n        r1 = min(r1, r2);\n        r2 = cal(x[l + 1] - n) + l + 1;\n        return min(r1, r2);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    \n    x[1] = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i <= 15; i++) {\n        x[i] = x[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < 7; i++) {\n        a[i] = i;\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 7; i < 1111110; i++) {\n        a[i] = cal(i);\n        now = i;\n    }\n    \n    if (n < 1111110) {\n        printf(\"%d\\n\", a[n]);\n    } else {\n        printf(\"%d\\n\", cal(n));\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nunordered_map<long long, int> memo;\n\nint solve(long long n) {\n    if (n < 0) n = -n;\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    if (n == 1) return 1;\n    \n    if (memo.find(n) != memo.end()) {\n        return memo[n];\n    }\n    \n    // Count digits and get first digit\n    long long temp = n;\n    int digits = 0;\n    while (temp > 0) {\n        digits++;\n        temp /= 10;\n    }\n    \n    // Get first digit\n    temp = n;\n    while (temp >= (long long)pow(10, digits-1)) {\n        temp /= 10;\n    }\n    int first_digit = temp;\n    \n    // Create number with all 1s of length digits\n    long long all_ones = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < digits; i++) {\n        all_ones = all_ones * 10 + 1;\n    }\n    \n    int result = INT_MAX;\n    \n    // Option 1: Use first_digit copies of all_ones\n    if (first_digit > 0) {\n        long long subtract = all_ones * first_digit;\n        if (subtract <= n) {\n            result = min(result, solve(n - subtract) + first_digit * digits);\n        } else {\n            result = min(result, solve(subtract - n) + first_digit * digits);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Option 2: Use (first_digit+1) copies of all_ones (if beneficial)\n    if (first_digit < 9) {\n        long long next_ones = all_ones * 10 + 1; // number with digits+1 ones\n        result = min(result, solve(next_ones - n) + (digits + 1));\n    }\n    \n    // Option 3: Use (first_digit-1) copies of all_ones\n    if (first_digit > 1) {\n        long long subtract = all_ones * (first_digit - 1);\n        result = min(result, solve(n - subtract) + (first_digit - 1) * digits);\n    }\n    \n    memo[n] = result;\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    \n    cout << solve(n) << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0006137394811958075, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00016211149340961128, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -4.9828242481453344e-05, 0.0, -3.659658250398934e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -3.3378546504536644e-06, 0.0, -0.005835757125169039, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.3385111689567566, -0.0002044230350293219, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.04859175905585289, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -0.5647562146186829, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -0.0008117241668514907, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.2330349087715149, -4.410734163684538e-06, -5.2689116273541003e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.005233872216194868, -7.390948667307384e-06, -0.0043028867803514, -0.0013268723851069808, -0.007501173764467239, -0.45574629306793213, -7.6293